<p>Bayerische Vereinsbank self-led with Hambros Bank as joint-lead manager a A$100 million Eurobond off its MTN programme on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The bonds, which mature June 30, 2000, pay a 6.50 percent coupon and carry a 100.74 issue price. Payment date is June 30.</p>
<p>Toyota Finance Australia also issued a A$150 million Eurobond due July 3, 2001 through BZW.</p>
<p>The bonds pay a 7.0 percent coupon and carry a 101.655 issue price. Payment date is July 3.</p>
